{
  "india-approved-15-lakh-crore-in": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Sansad_Bhavan%2C_Delhi%2C_BNK.jpg/960px-Sansad_Bhavan%2C_Delhi%2C_BNK.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"The old Sansad Bhavan (Parliament House) in New Delhi, whose written answers to Lok Sabha and Rajya Sabha questions supply this piece's PLI disbursement figures\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">Parliament's own written answers, not press releases, are the source for the disbursement figures in this piece. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sansad_Bhavan,_Delhi,_BNK.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sansad Bhavan, Delhi, BNK</a>, Nikhil B, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "the-currency-rupee-trends-piece-left": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/%E2%82%B92000_Indian_Rupee_Banknote.jpg/960px-%E2%82%B92000_Indian_Rupee_Banknote.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"A ₹2000 Indian rupee banknote, the currency whose ten-year exchange-rate history against the yen and five other currencies this piece charts\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">The rupee is the common thread across all six currency comparisons in this piece, including the yen, the one that moved the other way. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E2%82%B92000_Indian_Rupee_Banknote.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">₹2000 Indian Rupee Banknote</a>, Ravi Dwivedi, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "indias-coal-to-chemicals-menu-ranked-by": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Open_%28visible%29_Coal_Mines.jpg/960px-Open_%28visible%29_Coal_Mines.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"An open-cast coal mine in Jharkhand, India, the kind of high-ash domestic coal this piece says complicates India's coal-to-chemicals gasification push\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">India's coal is cheap, but its high ash content is exactly the handicap this piece says makes gasification harder here than it was for China. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Open_(visible)_Coal_Mines.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open (visible) Coal Mines</a>, Harshaddu, CC BY 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "indias-textile-import-export-strategy": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/32/Jamnagar_Refinery.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\" alt=\"Reliance's Jamnagar refinery and petrochemical complex in Gujarat, the naphtha-cracker route this piece says ethanol-freed feedstock could feed at national scale\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">Jamnagar already runs the naphtha-cracker and reformer chemistry this piece says ethanol blending could free up for polyester and PET feedstock nationally. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jamnagar_Refinery.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Jamnagar Refinery</a>, Reliance Industries, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "the-levelised-cost-of-hydrogen": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Astonfield_11.5MW_Solar_Plant_Gujarat.jpg/960px-Astonfield_11.5MW_Solar_Plant_Gujarat.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"A solar power plant in Gujarat, India, the state modelled as the base case for the renewable electricity feeding this piece's green-hydrogen cost calculations\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">Renewable electricity price and plant utilisation, not subsidy alone, are the two levers this piece says matter most for closing India's green-hydrogen cost gap. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Astonfield_11.5MW_Solar_Plant_Gujarat.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Astonfield 11.5MW Solar Plant Gujarat</a>, Citizenmj, CC BY-SA 3.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "sugar-at-5570-kilo-why-cane-acreage": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Transportation_of_sugarcane_from_field_to_Factory.jpg/960px-Transportation_of_sugarcane_from_field_to_Factory.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"Sugarcane being transported from field to mill in Maharashtra, one of the two states driving this season's record sugar output\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">Whether this cane becomes sugar or ethanol now turns on price, not policy — Maharashtra is one of the two states driving this season's output. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Transportation_of_sugarcane_from_field_to_Factory.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Transportation of sugarcane from field to Factory</a>, Shailaja jadhavpatil, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "where-indias-gigawatt-data-centre-bets": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Chennai_Port_aerial_view.jpg/960px-Chennai_Port_aerial_view.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"Aerial view of Chennai Port, the city this piece identifies as India's densest submarine-cable landing point and the anchor of its data-centre build-out\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">Chennai's advantage is under the sea as much as on land — six cables and 14.8 Tbps of capacity are why so many gigawatt-scale bets cluster here. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chennai_Port_aerial_view.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Chennai Port aerial view</a>, Saiphani02, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "re-spinning-charkha": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Charkha_%28spinning_wheel%291.jpg/960px-Charkha_%28spinning_wheel%291.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"A giant wooden charkha, the traditional hand-spinning wheel that gives this piece on Reliance's backward integration its title\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">Gandhi's charkha and Reliance's refineries share one goal, a century apart: stop paying someone else for the thread. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Charkha_(spinning_wheel)1.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Charkha (spinning wheel)1</a>, Janak Bhatta, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "india-has-tax-treaties-with-97": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/North_Block%2C_Raisina_Hill%2C_New_Delhi_01.jpg/960px-North_Block%2C_Raisina_Hill%2C_New_Delhi_01.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"North Block on Raisina Hill, New Delhi, seat of India's Finance Ministry, whose CBDT database and DGFT records supply this piece's tax- and trade-treaty counts\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">The 97-country tax-treaty count in this piece comes from a live database maintained here — the trade-treaty count from a much newer, much shorter list. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:North_Block,_Raisina_Hill,_New_Delhi_01.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">North Block, Raisina Hill, New Delhi 01</a>, Pinakpani, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "indias-used-oil-epr-wants-half-of-all": {
    "picture_html": null,
    "picture_note": "No topically strong, properly licensed photo could be found for India's used-oil/lubricant recycling EPR scheme specifically. Wikimedia Commons searches for used motor oil, lubricant drums, recycling facilities, and roadside garages/mechanics either returned non-photo results (PDFs, reports), a branded product-advertisement image, or photos from the wrong country (e.g. a Nigeria-tagged roadside mechanic shop from Wiki Loves Africa) that would misrepresent the India-specific subject if captioned as such. Rather than force an unrelated or miscaptioned image, this is left null per the task's fallback instruction."
  },
  "ten-cubic-metres-hour-indias-first": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e8/A_view_of_Tuticorin_Port.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\" alt=\"V.O. Chidambaranar Port at Tuticorin, Tamil Nadu, site of India's first port-based green hydrogen pilot and its shore-to-ship methanol bunkering trial\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">This port's 10-cubic-metre-an-hour hydrogen pilot currently powers streetlights, not ships — the gap this piece maps between paper-ready rules and physical scale. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_view_of_Tuticorin_Port.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">A view of Tuticorin Port</a>, Pearljose, CC BY-SA 3.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "indias-ethanol-surplus-isnt-going-to": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Working_in_the_shadow_of_an_Indian_sugar_mill.jpg/960px-Working_in_the_shadow_of_an_Indian_sugar_mill.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"Cane-sugar processing at a mill in Uttar Pradesh, India's largest sugar- and ethanol-feedstock-producing state\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">India's administered ethanol price already beats what Brazil or the U.S. would pay on the world market — which is why this surplus has nowhere profitable to export to. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Working_in_the_shadow_of_an_Indian_sugar_mill.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Working in the shadow of an Indian sugar mill</a>, Janoux, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  }
}